WEBVTT

00:16.495 --> 00:20.750
BLUE BOX SEASON 2

02:04.854 --> 02:07.273
Wow, great shot!
As expected from my daughter.

02:07.982 --> 02:08.983
You know it.

02:10.067 --> 02:12.611
Yumeka. You love basketball?

02:14.822 --> 02:16.114
Of course I do!

02:16.115 --> 02:17.824
More than you love your dad?

02:17.825 --> 02:20.035
Shut up.

02:25.166 --> 02:28.544
Listen, Yumeka.
Remember to treasure these moments.

02:30.629 --> 02:32.131
'Cause the strongest feeling

02:33.132 --> 02:35.801
is finding something you truly love.

02:36.677 --> 02:38.971
Mmm.

02:39.638 --> 02:41.931
That means you're strong too, Dad.

02:41.932 --> 02:43.850
Because you love Mom so much.

02:43.851 --> 02:47.354
That's right.
I love you and your mom a bunch!

02:49.064 --> 02:50.482
I love you.

03:00.326 --> 03:01.827
Sorry for bothering you.

03:09.668 --> 03:11.669
KIKUCHI DENTAL CLINIC

03:11.670 --> 03:13.172
<i>You're not wrong.</i>

03:14.548 --> 03:16.592
<i>I've been pushing everything on you.</i>

03:17.676 --> 03:20.428
<i>I decided not to continue basketball,</i>

03:20.429 --> 03:22.056
<i>and I took that out on you.</i>

03:27.561 --> 03:30.689
Wow. She's a first year,
but she made the team.

03:31.232 --> 03:34.317
She was a big deal
when she was in elementary school.

03:34.318 --> 03:39.030
That's amazing.
Although she doesn't look like it.

03:39.031 --> 03:39.907
<i>Damn it!</i>

03:40.616 --> 03:42.367
<i>It's not like I was arrogant,</i>

03:42.368 --> 03:44.787
<i>but I had my hands full just keeping up.</i>

03:45.329 --> 03:48.916
<i>I shouldn't be surprised.
They've got one or two years on me.</i>

03:57.508 --> 04:00.468
<i>I guess the talent that made me good
in elementary school</i>

04:00.469 --> 04:02.346
<i>won't be enough from now on.</i>

04:07.434 --> 04:08.560
Kido.

04:09.186 --> 04:11.313
I expect you'll do a lot better next time.

04:14.108 --> 04:15.067
Yes.

04:15.859 --> 04:19.071
<i>Okay. I just need to get better.</i>

04:20.030 --> 04:22.825
<i>I have to practice as much as I can,
like Natsu does.</i>

04:23.909 --> 04:26.577
<i>I'm here because
they expect me to play well.</i>

04:26.578 --> 04:28.330
<i>I need to work to prove them right.</i>

04:32.793 --> 04:35.671
<i>I need to work
until I can taste blood in my mouth.</i>

04:36.672 --> 04:39.091
<i>Until the sweat disappears from my hands.</i>

04:47.016 --> 04:49.935
<i>Until my heart beats so hard
that it bursts.</i>

04:59.361 --> 05:03.032
<i>I'll keep working
until I have nothing left to give.</i>

05:04.616 --> 05:06.075
Why can't you think

05:06.076 --> 05:07.160
- about family?
- I'm home.

05:07.161 --> 05:08.619
Really? This again?

05:08.620 --> 05:11.372
I know you're busy,
but you need to listen me.

05:11.373 --> 05:12.582
This is important.

05:12.583 --> 05:14.500
Didn't we just talk about this?

05:14.501 --> 05:17.671
You don't think about Yumeka or me at all.

05:18.213 --> 05:20.882
- You're the reason this family is...
- It's my fault?

05:20.883 --> 05:23.343
- There you go, shouting at me.
- Oh, and you aren't shouting?

05:23.344 --> 05:25.720
I can't do this. No matter what I say,

05:25.721 --> 05:27.681
- I can't get through to you.
- That's not true.

05:33.479 --> 05:37.941
<i>So that's how it goes.
All feelings change eventually.</i>

05:42.029 --> 05:44.113
Oh! Did you get your nails done?

05:44.114 --> 05:45.490
- Yeah, I did.
- I see.

05:45.491 --> 05:47.201
Do you think they look good on me?

05:47.743 --> 05:52.331
<i>Sorry, Dad.
I can feel my power weakening too.</i>

05:54.291 --> 05:56.585
<i>But I'll be okay, won't I?</i>

05:57.878 --> 06:01.090
<i>It's just that all the hard practice
is weighing me down.</i>

06:03.384 --> 06:06.720
<i>But my power will come back soon, right?</i>

06:15.646 --> 06:18.190
Oh, good morning, Yumeka! Join me!

06:21.235 --> 06:22.986
You're early, as usual.

06:25.072 --> 06:26.323
Come practice with me.

06:33.997 --> 06:36.708
<i>I have to make sure
Natsu doesn't find out.</i>

06:37.584 --> 06:40.629
<i>If she starts to feel defeated
because of me,</i>

06:41.338 --> 06:42.256
<i>I'd hate that.</i>

06:48.429 --> 06:50.764
<i>Because Natsu loves basketball.</i>

06:53.016 --> 06:56.477
<i>During a game, no one cares
about how hard you've worked.</i>

06:56.478 --> 06:58.104
Rebound! Nice!

06:58.105 --> 06:59.231
Yumeka!

07:00.607 --> 07:05.028
<i>Still, the confidence of knowing
you've worked hard becomes strength.</i>

07:06.488 --> 07:08.031
<i>No matter what,</i>

07:08.824 --> 07:10.451
<i>I have to make this shot.</i>

07:11.160 --> 07:13.036
<i>If I do that, then maybe...</i>

07:16.206 --> 07:20.043
<i>But how can I? When compared to her?</i>

07:46.028 --> 07:50.115
<i>Why? Why didn't I practice more?</i>

07:53.035 --> 07:55.954
<i>Why didn't I take basketball
more seriously?</i>

07:59.082 --> 08:01.418
<i>Am I gonna feel like this forever?</i>

08:03.962 --> 08:06.340
<i>What has all of my hard work been for?</i>

08:09.843 --> 08:11.178
<i>This isn't fun.</i>

08:12.971 --> 08:14.473
<i>I'm exhausted.</i>

08:17.851 --> 08:20.604
<i>Why am I working so hard?</i>

08:40.082 --> 08:41.250
Yumeka?

08:43.377 --> 08:45.003
I need to talk to you about something.

08:46.797 --> 08:49.258
Huh? I was still sleeping.

08:51.176 --> 08:53.512
- So, listen...
- What is it?

08:55.639 --> 08:58.475
Me and your dad are getting a divorce.

09:02.229 --> 09:04.606
That means he's not the strongest anymore.

09:17.286 --> 09:18.453
<i>Help me!</i>

09:24.876 --> 09:29.298
<i>All I want is to play basketball
like I used to.</i>

09:30.882 --> 09:34.803
<i>Back when I was so happy
just to make a shot.</i>

09:39.182 --> 09:41.435
<i>I don't wanna admit to myself...</i>

09:58.702 --> 10:01.872
<i>that maybe the truth is,</i>

10:02.873 --> 10:03.915
<i>I don't...</i>

10:04.916 --> 10:07.336
<i>love basketball anymore.</i>

10:25.854 --> 10:27.314
<i>The pain didn't stop.</i>

10:28.440 --> 10:31.193
<i>As I kept growing more and more negative,</i>

10:31.818 --> 10:33.862
<i>Natsu kept moving forward.</i>

10:36.156 --> 10:37.324
<i>I can't help but think...</i>

10:38.659 --> 10:39.576
Yumeka!

10:41.328 --> 10:44.081
<i>Maybe, if I had stayed by Natsu's side...</i>

10:46.667 --> 10:51.421
<i>I would've had the chance...
to love basketball again.</i>

10:58.011 --> 10:58.969
Huh?

10:58.970 --> 11:03.100
This is a ticket to Chinatsu's first game
at the Winter Cup.

11:04.518 --> 11:06.478
Yumeka, I'm giving it to you.

11:07.646 --> 11:10.649
This is a ticket to Chinatsu's first game
at the Winter Cup.

11:11.692 --> 11:13.734
Yumeka, I'm giving it to you.

11:13.735 --> 11:16.570
Please take it, and watch Chinatsu's game...

11:16.571 --> 11:18.114
You look exhausted.

11:18.115 --> 11:20.741
My legs are at their limit...

11:20.742 --> 11:23.494
You're "giving it" to me? But that's--

11:23.495 --> 11:25.747
It's because I have someone like him!

11:29.334 --> 11:31.335
Wouldn't it be better if you went?

11:31.336 --> 11:32.253
Huh?

11:32.254 --> 11:34.673
I know Natsu would be happier.

11:35.382 --> 11:36.800
It can't be me.

11:37.426 --> 11:40.053
When it comes to basketball,
it has to be you.

11:41.388 --> 11:43.597
And don't you think
it would be really nice

11:43.598 --> 11:46.560
to just go to the tournament
and watch an old friend play?

11:48.854 --> 11:52.398
Besides, I went through a lot of trouble
to get this ticket for you.

11:52.399 --> 11:53.775
Don't let it go to waste.

11:56.319 --> 11:57.362
I'm counting on you.

12:01.283 --> 12:02.701
Uh...

12:09.791 --> 12:11.125
I can't believe it.

12:11.126 --> 12:13.294
Who'd have thought a first year
would be so tough?

12:13.295 --> 12:16.214
Matsuoka must be so frustrated.

12:18.800 --> 12:21.177
Wow, you're really desperate.

12:21.178 --> 12:23.305
I wonder who you wanna
give this ticket to.

12:24.306 --> 12:26.015
Well, if you don't tell me now,

12:26.016 --> 12:28.893
I'll just ask the girls
on the basketball team later.

12:28.894 --> 12:29.728
That's cheating!

12:32.314 --> 12:34.064
I want it for Yumeka.

12:34.065 --> 12:35.275
Yumeka?

12:36.318 --> 12:38.611
She was on the basketball team
in middle school.

12:38.612 --> 12:39.988
Yeah, I know that, but...

12:40.572 --> 12:42.490
what does she have to do with any of this?

12:42.491 --> 12:44.825
- Huh?
- She already quit basketball.

12:44.826 --> 12:48.497
I bet it'd be hard for her
to watch someone play who didn't give up.

12:49.915 --> 12:52.501
And it's not like
she can come back to Eimei.

12:57.130 --> 12:58.006
You're right.

12:59.007 --> 13:01.510
Nothing I do can change what happened.

13:02.594 --> 13:05.846
But Yumeka isn't just someone
from Chinatsu's past.

13:05.847 --> 13:07.724
She's still a part of her.

13:10.018 --> 13:12.686
<i>The only reason Chinatsu is who she is</i>

13:12.687 --> 13:15.065
<i>is because she knew Yumeka growing up.</i>

13:16.858 --> 13:19.778
So I really want the two of them
to get along again.

13:22.489 --> 13:24.241
If that's selfish, so be it!

13:29.454 --> 13:32.040
So, how'd our first year do for himself?

13:32.624 --> 13:36.419
If you hadn't slipped on your own sweat,
I'm sure you could've kept running.

13:37.754 --> 13:39.171
I am stronger than him.

13:39.172 --> 13:41.006
Yeah? But did that matter?

13:41.007 --> 13:42.716
Don't try to hide it.

13:42.717 --> 13:46.096
You were already tired from running laps
this morning, weren't you?

13:47.264 --> 13:50.349
Even so, I've always been able
to rely on my strength.

13:50.350 --> 13:51.768
I thought I'd win anyway.

13:52.269 --> 13:54.937
That's a bad habit of yours, Matsuoka.

13:54.938 --> 13:56.189
Wait, really?

13:56.773 --> 13:58.858
Maybe if you were rested
and gave your all,

13:58.859 --> 14:01.068
you could have gotten something out of it.

14:01.069 --> 14:02.278
Hmm.

14:02.279 --> 14:05.240
I don't think that would have
made much of a difference.

14:06.741 --> 14:08.577
- All right, if you say so.
- Yeah.

14:23.633 --> 14:24.634
I'm off.

14:41.318 --> 14:43.028
- What's wrong?
- Huh?

14:43.820 --> 14:45.613
Oh, Chinatsu!

14:45.614 --> 14:48.866
Don't you have practice right now?
Why are you here?

14:48.867 --> 14:51.368
Oh, I just had... some things to do.

14:51.369 --> 14:53.914
I'm not skipping or anything.

14:54.873 --> 14:57.667
<i>I probably shouldn't tell her
about Yumeka.</i>

15:01.630 --> 15:02.672
Huh?

15:05.133 --> 15:07.134
What are you doing?

15:07.135 --> 15:10.013
It's just... I don't want you
to catch a cold again.

15:10.513 --> 15:12.222
But isn't that your towel?

15:12.223 --> 15:14.600
Well, it's a brand new one,
so don't worry.

15:14.601 --> 15:16.269
I'm not worried, it's just--

15:19.522 --> 15:20.439
TAKE IT

15:20.440 --> 15:22.817
All right, all right.
You don't have to say "I told you so."

15:28.698 --> 15:30.825
It's no biggie. Just wear my jacket.

15:34.412 --> 15:35.747
Are you copying me?

15:36.289 --> 15:37.832
I'm only returning the favor.

15:38.917 --> 15:41.877
You've given me so many things, Taiki.

15:41.878 --> 15:43.588
I have to give something back.

15:48.635 --> 15:50.845
What are you gonna offer me next?

15:51.721 --> 15:53.348
- Huh?
- I'm kidding.

15:54.724 --> 15:56.684
Uh...

15:56.685 --> 16:01.021
Oh, come on, it's just a joke!
Don't think too hard about it!

16:01.022 --> 16:02.899
<i>She's given me a lot too.</i>

16:03.692 --> 16:04.609
Listen...

16:06.027 --> 16:07.862
Whenever you're having a hard time,

16:08.697 --> 16:10.156
you can count on me.

16:21.084 --> 16:25.630
Since you said that,
from now on, I won't hesitate to ask.

16:27.465 --> 16:28.633
That's great.

16:30.510 --> 16:31.636
When the time comes,

16:32.637 --> 16:36.391
<i>whether it's at concert, the beach,
or anywhere else...</i>

16:37.183 --> 16:38.518
<i>I'll be by your side.</i>

16:44.065 --> 16:46.026
WINTER CUP
GO FOR THE GOLD!

16:54.409 --> 16:57.036
How is it December 23 already?

16:57.037 --> 16:59.371
You said the same thing
when December started.

16:59.372 --> 17:00.581
What do I do?

17:00.582 --> 17:03.876
I haven't been single on Christmas
since the fifth grade! It isn't right!

17:03.877 --> 17:05.127
Sounds young to be dating.

17:05.128 --> 17:08.130
You're acting all calm,
but you're single too, aren't you?

17:08.131 --> 17:09.757
Don't you feel the despair?

17:09.758 --> 17:10.842
No, not really.

17:11.634 --> 17:14.178
My family spends Christmas
together every year.

17:14.179 --> 17:15.095
Huh?

17:15.096 --> 17:16.597
I have three siblings,

17:16.598 --> 17:18.891
so it's a lot of work
to prepare all the food and stuff.

17:18.892 --> 17:19.808
Wait, three?

17:19.809 --> 17:22.729
Last year, we even had to get
two different types of cake!

17:25.815 --> 17:27.983
Aren't you spending Christmas
with your family too?

17:27.984 --> 17:29.943
Well, I'd like to, but...

17:29.944 --> 17:31.988
my sister usually has plans.

17:32.739 --> 17:34.615
Family's nothing to her!

17:34.616 --> 17:36.034
- Ayame!
- Huh?

17:37.118 --> 17:41.246
We were talking about going to karaoke
with everyone after practice tomorrow.

17:41.247 --> 17:42.248
Wanna come with?

17:43.041 --> 17:44.375
Hina bean!

17:45.085 --> 17:48.254
When all else fails,
you can count on friendship!

17:48.880 --> 17:50.798
Hina always chooses the best songs.

17:50.799 --> 17:52.550
I can't wait!

17:55.345 --> 17:57.930
Christmas Eve matters
not to us, right lad?

17:57.931 --> 17:58.765
Yeah...

18:00.850 --> 18:03.269
Practice is life!

18:04.771 --> 18:06.939
Hey, Taiki. Wanna come?

18:06.940 --> 18:07.774
Huh?

18:08.399 --> 18:11.277
We're all going together
to Christmas karaoke tomorrow.

18:15.907 --> 18:17.199
Sorry.

18:17.200 --> 18:20.369
I promised to get in
some extra practice with Nishida.

18:20.370 --> 18:23.748
He wants the guys
to do strength training on Christmas Eve.

18:24.874 --> 18:25.917
Okay!

18:26.960 --> 18:30.379
Well, let's leave strength training
to the freaks and have a blast!

18:30.380 --> 18:31.297
Sounds good!

18:32.048 --> 18:34.383
- Is Hina a good singer?
- Seriously.

18:34.384 --> 18:36.552
When Hina starts singing,
it's like a concert!

18:36.553 --> 18:38.555
Come on, Niina, don't exaggerate.

18:39.264 --> 18:40.639
Well, see you tomorrow.

18:40.640 --> 18:41.891
See you tomorrow.

18:43.184 --> 18:45.061
All right, team, listen up!

18:45.687 --> 18:47.896
Let's stay focused
for the Winter Cup tomorrow.

18:47.897 --> 18:49.022
Yeah!

18:49.023 --> 18:50.899
Don't let the cold get to you.

18:50.900 --> 18:51.859
Yeah!

18:51.860 --> 18:54.027
Set your desire to win on fire.

18:54.028 --> 18:55.028
Yeah!

18:55.029 --> 18:57.114
Let's go, Eimei!

18:57.115 --> 18:58.782
Yeah!

18:58.783 --> 19:01.034
So the girls have a game tomorrow.

19:01.035 --> 19:02.161
At what time?

19:02.162 --> 19:03.620
Around 1:00 p.m., I think.

19:03.621 --> 19:05.206
Do your best!

19:05.915 --> 19:06.916
Thank you.

19:08.543 --> 19:09.710
- Best of luck.
- Thank you.

19:09.711 --> 19:10.794
- Do your best.
- Thank you.

19:10.795 --> 19:12.213
- Thank you.
- Thank you!

19:26.311 --> 19:28.520
Is it okay if we meet at 1:00 tomorrow?

19:28.521 --> 19:29.438
Huh?

19:29.439 --> 19:31.440
For our Christmas date, silly.

19:31.441 --> 19:33.942
First, we can buy each other presents,

19:33.943 --> 19:36.069
then go to a café with good coffee,

19:36.070 --> 19:38.280
and finish by seeing the Christmas lights.

19:38.281 --> 19:41.033
- This one place has amazing lights.
- Hey, uh, Sosuke...

19:41.034 --> 19:44.370
And if you can, it'd be great
if you wore your knee-high socks.

19:44.954 --> 19:46.497
I'm just kidding.

19:47.207 --> 19:49.124
I'm going to the bathroom.

19:49.125 --> 19:50.001
Okay.

19:50.919 --> 19:53.004
Huh... Huh?

20:01.346 --> 20:02.429
Oh that's--

20:02.430 --> 20:03.264
Wait a minute.

20:04.015 --> 20:07.100
A ticket to tomorrow's winter cup game?

20:07.101 --> 20:09.102
Wait, you have to go!

20:09.103 --> 20:11.438
You'd see that girl
from the other day, right?

20:11.439 --> 20:12.940
And don't worry about me.

20:12.941 --> 20:15.193
We can totally go on our date
after the game.

20:15.902 --> 20:17.069
Why are you standing?

20:17.070 --> 20:18.821
- Come on. Sit down.
- 'Kay.

20:20.365 --> 20:22.950
By the way, what did you write
as your dream for the future

20:22.951 --> 20:25.036
in your elementary school yearbook?

20:25.620 --> 20:26.536
Uh...

20:26.537 --> 20:28.039
DREAM
BASKETBALL PLAYER

20:28.665 --> 20:30.249
I wanted to be a soccer player.

20:30.250 --> 20:31.625
I didn't know that.

20:31.626 --> 20:34.127
Yeah. I'd completely
forgotten about it, too.

20:34.128 --> 20:38.091
That dream went away on its own.
I never consciously gave it up.

20:39.384 --> 20:40.717
But maybe,

20:40.718 --> 20:44.555
because you had a clearer goal in mind
when playing basketball,

20:45.181 --> 20:48.643
<i>you seem to be unsure
about how to act towards it now.</i>

20:51.145 --> 20:53.064
How should I put it?

20:53.648 --> 20:54.648
When this happens,

20:54.649 --> 20:57.150
you have to strip away
the unnecessary things.

20:57.151 --> 20:58.069
Strip away?

20:59.112 --> 21:00.696
<i>As we live our lives,</i>

21:00.697 --> 21:04.701
<i>painful difficult things have a way
of getting stuck to the fun things.</i>

21:07.370 --> 21:10.038
<i>If you strip away
the difficult things one by one</i>

21:10.039 --> 21:11.457
<i>and look at what's left,</i>

21:13.209 --> 21:16.670
don't you still love basketball?

21:16.671 --> 21:17.547
Hmm?

21:25.930 --> 21:29.976
As it turns out, your obsession
might not actually be such a bad thing.

21:33.187 --> 21:34.856
Oh, there it is.

21:35.565 --> 21:37.941
When you don't want people to know
what you're thinking,

21:37.942 --> 21:39.693
you mess with your bangs.

21:39.694 --> 21:41.738
- What?
- Didn't you know?

21:43.448 --> 21:45.867
<i>Life presents us with challenges.</i>

21:46.492 --> 21:49.620
<i>For some people,
it's easier to deal with them.</i>

21:50.705 --> 21:51.955
<i>It's okay to quit.</i>

21:51.956 --> 21:54.125
<i>It's okay to not push yourself so hard.</i>

22:04.594 --> 22:08.389
<i>But don't forget that sense of excitement.</i>

22:09.390 --> 22:11.142
<i>Be confident in what you love.</i>

22:15.813 --> 22:16.898
<i>'Cause by doing that,</i>

22:18.274 --> 22:20.234
<i>you'll be the strongest you can be.</i>

22:20.985 --> 22:23.905
EPISODE 29
LOVE IS THE MOST POWERFUL FEELING
